+# FAA's native AA77 inventory and flight-path analysis
+
+October 27, 2026. Original-record acquisition and testing; existing AUD016-A1 / TC01–TC04. These records advance radar/voice custody and reconstruction questions. They do not complete the separate FAA correction and administrative-disposition questions PD01–PD04.
+
+Two native Word files have now been acquired directly from the National Archives' public catalog. The most useful result is a set of specific source-media and transfer-record leads, together with the FAA analysis's own limitations. There is also a preserved difference between the inventory's 2001 body date and its 2006 stored document dates. None of these observations establishes fabricated radar data, deliberate concealment or a conspiracy.
+
+## Sources and reading scope
+
+| ID | Official source | Acquired bytes / SHA-256 |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| I | [NARA 7597271](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7597271), [native inventory DOC](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/2-UAL-93/e-Other/2-ZID-24-INVENTORY-OF-AAL77-DATA.DOC) | 43,520 / `7f3d2f6827c1f639c46405b13b3e56e8dc2cef66bf11b426492d885a6a1cd002` |
+| A | [NARA 7596609](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7596609), [native analysis DOC](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/1-AAL-77/e-Other/1-ZID-74-AAL77a_ZID.doc) | 23,040 / `c6ae671a99d6aaa68dfabd23caef25f3d72516afc0dd6bcdf10a34e2d657e7ad` |
+
+Access: October 27, 2026, approximately 18:29 UTC. Both actual responses were HTTP 200, `application/msword`, with OLE compound-file signatures. The catalog supplies the public download links and labels use unrestricted; its series-level access note also warns that some FAA records are redacted. Acquisition receipts preserve these statements separately. Official hosting establishes where this copy came from; it does not authenticate every event or stored property in it.
+
+All extracted text was read: 199 physical lines for I and 39 for A. Locators below refer to these saved textutil extractions, not original page numbers. [SOURCE-EXCERPTS.json](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.json) preserves selected exact lines and extraction hashes. Read-only textutil text/WordML conversions, an OLE stream/property audit and first-page Quick Look thumbnails were used. The thumbnails visually confirm I's heading/date and initial inventory entries, and A's analysis and QRI spelling. They are not a full paginated rendering. Trailing `PAGE 4` / `PAGE 2` extraction fields are not used as pagination evidence. Native revisions, comments, embedded objects and macros have not received a complete Word-binary forensic audit.
+
+## Observations and their limits
+
+**1. The inventory names actual transfer records and source media.** I lines 89–101 list certified accident-file cassettes and HNN R/RA copies for **NTSB request 01-096**. Lines 180–185 identify a fax receipt/overnight package for R95 and D95 voice copies, that request, an updated September 25 radar request and a CC-Mail account of material sent through a website. Lines 175–176 identify two CDs labeled `ZID-AAL77.WAVE`, received September 20, with contents reportedly sent to ATH-200. These are inventory assertions. The actual request, receipt, message, CDs and successful recipient acknowledgment were not acquired in this unit. Listing them does not complete custody or prove what survives today.
+
+**2. There is a limited identifier/time join to the NTAP original already held.** I line 24 lists SAR tape **1635**, `1234-1258 UTC`; I line 44 gives the last transponder hit as **1256:19 UTC [350]**. The independently acquired [NARA NTAP 7596008](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7596008), SHA-256 `5409296c7834e0e834f201e6b78bc43042a2920053af49c243384ded9a5f3f0e`, identifies input tape 1635 and has a final code-3743 LST3 entry at printed **1256:19**, raw ALT **350**. [IDENTIFIER-JOINS.json](IDENTIFIER-JOINS.json) checks the held bytes and previous row extraction. This supports a candidate source relationship. It is not byte identity with the original tape, a complete chain of custody, authenticated altitude units, independently established aircraft identity or clock calibration. The NTAP print does not itself explicitly label its timebase UTC.
+
+**3. Different voice and replay objects have different windows.** I lines 7–8 list reel 1072's R95 `1239-1304 UTC` and D95 `1257-1316 UTC`. A draft R95 transcript is labeled `1238-1320 UTC` at line 62. Work SATORI VOX cassettes at lines 107–109 are `1247-1259` and `1257-1308 UTC`, while named SATORI files at lines 112–114 are `1248-1258`, `1258-1308` and `1308-1318 UTC`; the third is explicitly **No VOX**. Lines 115–119 describe destinations and a September 24 DAT copy. Preserve every label. These are different named objects, not yet matched samples of one recording. Their differing windows do not by themselves demonstrate removed audio. The previously published ATC report's other windows and timecode-reader statement remain unchanged and unresolved; original audio, channel maps, copy logs and reader worksheets are needed for an actual overlap/alignment test.
+
+**4. The FAA memo expressly limits its reconstruction.** A line 15 identifies approximate endpoints **12:56:19Z** and **13:04:32Z**. It says this office lacked radar-analysis certification while periodically analyzing HOST/NAS data. Line 17 describes manual work by specialists, contractors and Air Force personnel and calls the route an approximation, not an exact path. Lines 19–23 distinguish QHY beacon-only coverage, inconclusive QRI primary data and useful recorded QBE data from what controllers could see. The memo says no radar data was available to controllers between its endpoints, while reconstruction used other sources not ordinarily displayed to them. This is important source-defined scope: recorded returns and a controller display are separate questions. We have not independently tested those statements or used them to adjudicate a broader claim that radar data were absent everywhere. The office's qualification statement does not establish that the later NTSB radar study was performed by unqualified staff. The attached depiction and its point-to-return worksheet have not been independently joined to these DOC bytes.
+
+**5. Several apparent absences require their own definitions.** I lines 35 and 45–48 label some DART/NTAP outputs blank and another primary output “Some data.” Line 4 labels reel 1062 **9/12/01**, describes AA77 and UA93 data and says it had recently been discovered and was still being researched. Other reels are labeled 9/11/01. The catalog places I under UAL93 Other while its body/title concern AAL77. Preserve each statement without assuming misfiling, a wrong recording date, deliberate delay or destruction. Blank query output is not proof that the underlying system recorded nothing. The actual query controls, reel labels, discovery notes and accession description are the discriminating records.
+
+**6. The inventory's body date differs from its stored properties.** I line 2 says **“UP DATED 09/27/01.”** In `SummaryInformation`, PID 12 (creation) and PID 13 (last save) both encode **2006-04-11 13:10:00 UTC**. Property/value logical stream offsets are respectively **432/436** and **444/448**; both eight-byte values are `0044d23c695dc601`. A instead has body date September 17, 2001 and stored creation/save dates **2001-09-17 18:53 / 19:01 UTC**. All four dates agree between textutil, olefile and direct FILETIME decoding. [NATIVE-PROPERTY-AUDIT.json](NATIVE-PROPERTY-AUDIT.json) retains the exact ticks, bytes and offsets. These offsets are within the property stream, not the physical DOC file. Microsoft's [property specification](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/openspecs/windows_protocols/ms-oleps/f7933d28-2cc4-4b36-bc23-8861cbcd37c4) defines the fields; it does not authenticate them. Later saving, release processing or other editing are untested possible causes. We do not select one. This does not date the original inventory's authorship to 2006, identify an editor, or demonstrate fabrication. An earlier hashed copy, accession history and processing/version records could test the difference.
+
+## Priority originals still needed
+
+1. NTSB 01-096, the September 25 update, complete fax/overnight receipts and CC-Mail/website transfer manifests, then recipient-side inventories and actual retained copies.
+2. R95/D95 masters and certified copies, `ZID-AAL77.WAVE`, all three SATORI files, DAT/copy logs, channel mappings and timecode-reader calibration/verification worksheets. “No VOX” must remain a label until the actual file and channel contents are inspected.
+3. SAR 1635 and 1045, raw QBE/QRI outputs, query settings, the attached flight-path grid and point-to-return/source-association worksheets. Only then can the reconstruction and clocks be independently tested.
+4. Inventory accession/version and release-processing records, and the records concerning reel 1062's date and discovery. No allegation of improper editing follows merely from the metadata difference.
+
+The strongest objection to treating this as evidence of concealment is that the inventory openly identifies media, certified copies and transfers, and the analysis openly qualifies its reconstruction. Those records could support ordinary copying and release processing. That alternative remains a hypothesis, not a resolved explanation. Conversely, an inventory and a qualification paragraph cannot substitute for the missing underlying records or establish that transfers/calibration were correctly performed.
+
+## Verification and preservation
+
+`inspect_native_properties.py` opens both sources read-only, verifies their hashes, lists logical streams and independently decodes the two standard time properties. It does not execute document content. No parsing issues were reported within this narrow scope; that is not a clean bill of health for all Word internals. Six textutil conversions succeeded with unchanged inputs; two first-page thumbnails were generated and inspected. Actual checks and limits are in VERIFICATION.json and CHECKLIST.json. Earlier reports, conflicting values and source bytes remain unchanged. Exact text additions are preserved under diffs/; layout review is separate.
+
+Only selected public-source excerpts, research notes, safe structural properties and reproducibility artifacts form this publication payload. Native DOC files, full conversions and thumbnails remain preserved in the verified source store. Source links and hashes allow readers to obtain the agency-hosted bytes. No contact, new records request, fee, case-record change or private-repository push occurred. The five-track goal remains active and incomplete.
